<h2 id="ha-ctrl-013-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Review the owner, administrator and non-administrator views with permitted test accounts. Check that Home Assistant rejects a forbidden action whether or not the control is visible.
2. Change an account preference and a browser-only preference in two clients. Record how each persists and what sign-out does.
3. Expire a session and remove a permission while an edit is open. No rejected or unconfirmed change may be labelled saved.
4. Check keyboard access, private fields and the scope shown on a shared display. Keep tokens, secrets and personal locations out of public evidence.

Record the Home Assistant version, the browser, the fixture or device, the starting state, the expected and observed results, and where the evidence is kept. A documentation check is not a live-device test.

For personal preferences see [Settings and preferences](../patterns/settings.html). For rejected requests see [Action requests and results](action-results.html).

